 ## Deferred from: code review Round 2 of 3-4-routing-visit-loop-hardening (2026-06-14)
 
 - **Silent rejection of an invalid review photo** *(Target: Story 8.4 — Feedback & Review Persistence Enablement)* — when `isSafeOptionalPhoto` rejects a pick (oversized >5 MB, non-`image/*`, 0-byte, or name >120 chars) the handler calls `setPhoto(undefined)` and clears the input without writing anything to the always-mounted `role="status"` region, so no user (sighted or screen-reader) is told the photo was refused — the Camera button just appears to do nothing. Pre-existing from Story 3.3; Round 2 of Story 3.4 only added the announcement region. Fix needs a localized rejection string surfaced in the same status region; fold it in when real photo persistence reworks the upload UX. [`nextjs-app/components/composed/feedback/ReviewForm.tsx:193-197,219-229`] **TARGETED 2026-06-14:** carry-in reflected under Story 8.4 in `epics.md`.
-- **`isVenueNotFoundError` couples 404 detection to the error string** *(Target: Story 8.2 — Real Venue Store & API)* — `/failed:\s404\b/i.test(error.message)` matches only the current `Venue detail failed: 404 Not Found` format (and mirrors the established 4xx convention), so any future change to how the fetch layer formats its error message silently breaks the not-found branch. Robust fix is to carry a numeric `status` on the thrown error and test against it; do this when the real venue API + error contract lands. [`nextjs-app/hooks/queries/venue-query-options.ts:427`] **TARGETED 2026-06-14:** carry-in reflected under Story 8.2 in `epics.md`.
+*(One entry — `isVenueNotFoundError` 404 detection coupled to the error-message string — carried into Story 8.2 — Real Venue Store & API (AC #4 / Task 4) on 2026-06-17. Removed by SM per the deferred-work convention.)*
 - **`messages-parity` ICU test checks argument names, not formatter types/styles** *(Target: None — conditional, only triggers if an ICU formatter-style sv/en drift is suspected)* — the test pins per-key ICU argument names (catching a dropped `{minutes}`) but not formatter type/style, so an sv/en drift like `{minutes, number, integer}` vs `{minutes}` passes. Enhancement only; the primary drop-an-argument risk is covered. [`nextjs-app/test/unit/messages-parity.test.ts`]
 - **`routing-boundary` test matching is brittle** *(Target: None — conditional, only triggers if a legitimate new routing consumer is blocked by the assertion)* — `.toEqual([...exact consumer paths])` forces an unrelated future story to edit the test on any legitimate new consumer, and the raw-text `includes('window.open(')` / native-URL pattern scans count occurrences inside comments or string literals as real matches. Deliberate boundary pin; tighten to ignore comments/strings and assert a subset/allowlist when next touched. [`nextjs-app/test/unit/routing-boundary.test.ts`]
 - **`VenueDetailError` lacks an actionless-combo invariant** *(Target: None — conditional, only triggers if the detail-error precedence logic is refactored)* — `{isNotFound:true, showBack:false}` would render an alert with neither a retry nor a back control. Currently unreachable (the sole call site always pairs `isNotFound:true` with `showBack:true`), but a future refactor of the precedence IIFE could strand the user. Add a `showBack || !isNotFound` guard (or always render Back) when the component is next touched. [`nextjs-app/components/custom/map/MapView.tsx:1380-1421`]
